From e75617ea199ad84b2e290548fe7d2f915854edcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Acquire canonical listed-card sets on caller-owned
 snapshots

Extract the existing execution-authority/detail/wait enrichment into one
connection-taking owner shared with the legacy session reader. Add complete
per-session creator/subscriber membership via JSON scopes rather than a
union-only or per-session query loop. Require captured gateway/profile scope
so cold identity discovery cannot open a hidden reader inside acquisition.
Borrow explicit parent replicas, including containment resolution; explicit
None is local-only. Legacy omitted replica arguments retain their ownership.

Size execution chunks for their double-bound IDs and details for their fixed
bindings. JSON-bound containment scopes retain every authority above the SQLite
999-variable cap. The new complete selector propagates operational subscriber
errors rather than certifying partial coverage; legacy optional reads retain
their existing failure boundary.

Why: an independently opened canonical reader cannot share a caller's cursor
snapshot; union dedup loses per-chat provenance; 500 twice-bound IDs exceed999.
These are acquisition boundaries, not changes to authority or outcome policy.

Proof: canonical RED/GREEN covers snapshot interleaving, physical SQLite open
instrumentation, borrowed replica closure, 4097 lineage IDs under limit999,
legacy/local/PRIMARY/unavailable and receipt differential controls, named owner
scope, explicit clock/CI/deploy waits, containment and foreign parent custody.
Focused suites and full scripts/check --base origin/main pass. Wider immutable
snapshot and clause-mutation evidence follows before publication/review.

No panel feed/store activation, reader DDL, persistent connections or claim of
bounded history scans. Rollback is a normal revert of this acquisition change.
